1. odd m = 2k+1 <= 401: centre block = [[d,-d],[-d,d]] with d = 4^-1, and 3d-1 = -d, 3(-d)+1 = d (mod m): 200/200
   m=9: k^2=7, k(k+1)=2, (k+1)^2=7; 4^-1=7, -4^-1=2; 3*7-1=2, 3*2+1=7
   m=11: k^2=3, k(k+1)=8, (k+1)^2=3; 4^-1=3, -4^-1=8; 3*3-1=8, 3*8+1=3
   m=13: k^2=10, k(k+1)=3, (k+1)^2=10; 4^-1=10, -4^-1=3; 3*10-1=3, 3*3+1=10
   m=15: k^2=4, k(k+1)=11, (k+1)^2=4; 4^-1=4, -4^-1=11; 3*4-1=11, 3*11+1=4
   m=21: k^2=16, k(k+1)=5, (k+1)^2=16; 4^-1=16, -4^-1=5; 3*16-1=5, 3*5+1=16
   even m = 2k, k odd, m <= 398: k^2 = k, (k+-1)^2 = k+1, (k-1)(k+1) = k-1 (mod m): 99/99; mod 10: 5,6,6,4 (the central 5 with 4 and 6 diagonalized); 3*4+1=3, 3*6-1=7: no stitching
2. mod 9: orbits of the full table under swap x sign flips: 15; block without the centre cross: 15 = T_5 = 15; representatives 0<=x<=y<=k: 15
2. mod 10: orbits of the full table under swap x sign flips: 21; block without the centre cross: 15 = T_5 = 15; representatives 0<=x<=y<=k: 15
2. mod 11: orbits of the full table under swap x sign flips: 21; block without the centre cross: 21 = T_6 = 21; representatives 0<=x<=y<=k: 21
3. triples (n, ceil(n/2), 2n+1), n <= 2000: 4y = +1 mod z and 3y-1 = -y on B (n odd), 4y = -1 and 3y+1 = -y on A (n even): 2000/2000
   p(B_k,A_k) = (z(B_k), 2N), p(A_k,B_k) = (z(B_k), 2N-1) with N = k(4k-1) = y z: 1000/1000 (the x-pair of the atom y*z)
   q(I, I+1) = (4I+1, 4I+4); for odd I the odd output is the sibling, U(4I+1) = U(I): 10000/10000
   sheet split: v2(3z+1) = 1 and v2(3z-1) >= 2 on B; v2(3z-1) = 1 and v2(3z+1) >= 2 on A: 10000/10000 (the P/M cases of the sibling automaton)
4. primes <= 10^6: in B (4k-1) 39322, in A (4k+1) 39175 (Chebyshev bias toward B: 147)
   valuation profile of 3z+1 (a=1..5, >=6) on A: primes [0.0, 0.4991, 0.2503, 0.1248, 0.063, 0.0627] vs all [0.0, 0.5, 0.25, 0.125, 0.0625, 0.0625]; on B of 3z-1: primes [0.0, 0.5002, 0.2502, 0.1251, 0.0623, 0.0621] vs all [0.0, 0.5, 0.25, 0.125, 0.0625, 0.0625] (geometric(1/2) beyond the forced first bit: primality does not see the sheets)
5. tournaments on 5 vertices: 1024 labelled, 12 isomorphism classes, 6 strong; fixed Hamiltonian path 1->2->3->4->5 leaves 6 off-path arcs in diagonals (by length 2,3,4): [3, 2, 1], so 2^6 = 64 tilings; a selfie 5-tournament has 10 arcs + 5 loops = 15 tiles = T_5, and the frame around the 6 off-path tiles is the 4 path arcs plus the 5 loops = 9
